# Every function here is about 'long double', which this backend has no
# register class for: it lives on the x87 stack, and section 10 of
# docs/ir-codegen-design.md has already decided to lower it to soft float
# rather than model x87 behind a register allocator built for a flat namespace.
#
# 'ldf' returns one and loads one; 'main' materializes long double constants
# and passes them; 't' converts to and from one as well.
#
# Delete this file when roadmap step 18 lands. -noFallback rejects a name
# listed here that stopped falling back, so it cannot outlive what it excuses.
ldf
main
t
